EnquiryForm lays out a proposal or service request: TextFields in two columns, choices, a message box and one submit button.

- Markup: `<form class="aq-form" novalidate>` holding `aq-field` blocks (see TextField). Fields that need the full width (message, checkbox groups) add `aq-form__full`. End with `<div class="aq-form__actions">` holding one `aq-btn--primary` and a `<span class="aq-small" role="status">` for the result message.
- Select: `<select class="aq-field__input">`. Message: `<textarea class="aq-field__input">`.
- Checkbox group: `<fieldset class="aq-fieldset aq-field aq-form__full">` with a `<legend class="aq-field__label">` and `<div class="aq-checks">` of `<label><input type="checkbox"> System type</label>`.
- Mark optional fields, not required ones: `<span class="aq-field__optional">(optional)</span>` inside the label.
- Ask what an engineer can answer: project stage, system type, required capacity in L/h, standards, timeline. Capacity and temperature use the unit suffix.
- The submit label says what happens: "Request a proposal", "Send service request". The consumer provides validation and submission.
